(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[17 1 "// Finalization (PYS9 (a); doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 218\"): pyi has no reference counts, so an object's"] [18 1 "// death is Go's collector's finding. A tracked object (one with weak references, or with a finalizer's work due: a"] [19 1 "// class's __del__, a generator's close, a socket's warning) has a Go finalizer and a record in tracked, keyed by its"] [20 1 "// address and never holding it. Go's finalizer goroutine only moves the dead object into finQueue and sets the eval"] [21 1 "// breaker's bit; the thread holding the GIL drains the queue (handleEvalBreaker, gc.collect). The order is reference"] [22 1 "// counting's (subtype_dealloc): the work first, the Go finalizer set again without it (PEP 442: once only); found"] [23 1 "// unreachable again, the weak references are cleared (in the Go finalizer, under finMu, so no weak reference yields"] [24 1 "// the object after it) and their callbacks called in CPython's list order. Go's heap does not move and an object with"] [25 1 "// a finalizer is kept until the finalizer ran, so a weak reference's hidden address is valid while it is not cleared."] [27 1 "// the work a tracked object's death runs"] [29 23 "// its class's __del__ (slot_tp_finalize)"] [30 23 "// a generator's, coroutine's or async generator's finalization (_PyGen_Finalize)"] [31 23 "// an open socket's ResourceWarning and close (sock_finalize)"] [32 23 "// an async generator's awaitable never awaited (async_gen_asend_finalize)"] [33 23 "// a built-in type's tp_finalize, the record's fin (TrackFinalizer, queue 241)"] [36 1 "// finTrack is a tracked object's record."] [38 21 "// the object's pointer's element type, to rebuild it from its address"] [39 21 "// its weak references in CPython's order: the basic ref, the basic proxy, then the newest first"] [40 21 "// the work due at its death"] [41 21 "// its identity once hashed (identityHash; an instance keeps it in its own field)"] [42 2 "// aioTask: a registered asyncio task past the strong list (builtins_asyncio.go's registry, queue 224)"] [44 2 "// owner is the interpreter that tracked it (queue 230): its work runs there, nil for the main one before any thread"] [46 2 "// fin is a built-in type's tp_finalize (workFin; queue 241), given the object: it must hold no reference to it"] [48 2 "// seq is the record's order of making (queue 253): a collection's trash is finalized in it, as CPython's lists"] [49 2 "// keep their objects in the order they were tracked"] [53 1 "// finSeq numbers the records (finMu)."] [56 1 "// finItem is a dead object's turn in the queue: obj and its work, or (obj nil) its weak references' callbacks."] [63 24 "// tracked, finQueue, the weak references' addresses (Go's finalizer goroutine takes it too)"] [66 26 "// the Go finalizers run so far (finBarrier's sign of progress)"] [67 26 "// a drain is running (under the GIL): a nested one leaves the queue to it"] [69 18 "// PYI_NO_FINALIZERS: nothing tracked (the weak references hold their referents, as before 218)"] [74 1 "// The moment at del (queue 222; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 222\"): DELETE_FAST of a tracked object with work"] [75 1 "// or weak references due asks Go's collector at once whether that was the last reference, and drains the queue before"] [76 1 "// the next instruction: reference counting's moment when it was, a wasted collection when it was not. The collections'"] [77 1 "// time is held to a tenth of the elapsed wall time (and 50 ms); past it the death waits for the next collection."] [83 1 "// finDeletedAt is DELETE_FAST of f's fast local i (not unbound) with the check of the value it deletes. The value is"] [84 1 "// read and cleared here and dropped before anything else runs: no other variable, and no frame of a call goi"] [85 1 "// interprets, keeps it (goi's registers keep a returned call's values: queue 218's REQUEST), so that the collection"] [86 1 "// can find it dead."] [104 1 "// finPeek is the address of the value of name in d, before DELETE_NAME or DELETE_GLOBAL deletes it (0: nothing to"] [105 1 "// check); the deletion's moment is then finDeleted's, as DELETE_FAST's (queue 224: `del g` at a module's level)."] [121 1 "// finAddr is o's address for finDeleted when its holder lets it go (0: nothing to check); queue 293: sys.settrace's and"] [122 1 "// sys.setprofile's previous function, the thread's only reference to it, whose __del__ CPython runs as the call"] [123 1 "// drops it (test_sys_settrace's test_reentrancy: a __del__ that sets the trace function)."] [135 1 "// finDeleted is the check of a deleted object at address a."] [150 1 "// finVerify is the collection at a deletion: rounds while the object's record moves (its work run, then its weak"] [151 1 "// references cleared: subtype_dealloc's two steps), each a Go collection and a wait until the record moved or Go's"] [152 1 "// finalizers have all run (finBarrier), then the drain."] [178 1 "// finQueued is whether tr's object is in the queue (finMu held)."] [188 1 "// addrOf is o's address (o a pointer: finTrackable)."] [191 1 "// hiddenPtr reads the address *u as a pointer (a weak reference's referent, alive while not cleared)."] [194 1 "// toObject is the object of type *elem at the address *u (a weak reference's referent; finMu held, *u not 0)."] [199 1 "// finTrackable is o's possible tracking: a pointer to a non-empty type of this package (another package's objects"] [200 1 "// may have their own Go finalizer, which a second SetFinalizer would abort on: _bz2's, _sqlite3's, _zstd's)."] [209 1 "// trackLocked is o's record, made (with its Go finalizer) when o has none; finMu held."] [228 1 "// trackWork tracks o (finTrackable) with the work w due at its death."] [239 1 "// TrackFinalizer is a built-in type's tp_finalize (queue 241): fin(o) runs under the GIL at o's death, once, in"] [240 1 "// __del__'s place in the order (a cycle's too). o is a pointer to a non-empty type with no Go finalizer of its own (a"] [241 1 "// type of another package may be given: pysqlite3's cursor); fin takes o as its argument and must hold no reference"] [242 1 "// to it (the record would keep it alive)."] [259 1 "// goFinalized is the Go finalizer of every tracked object, run on Go's finalizer goroutine: o into the queue."] [285 1 "// drainFinalizers runs the queue under the GIL until it is empty: the number of dead objects handled."] [312 4 "// its interpreter ended: no one to run the work in (queue 230)"] [337 2 "// the record stays (its Go finalizer set again) while weak references, new work or an identity need it"] [350 1 "// runWork runs the work w due at o's death (its record's work already cleared: PEP 442's once)."] [371 1 "// weakCallbacks calls the callbacks of a dead object's weak references, in its list's order (PyObject_ClearWeakRefs)."] [385 1 "// runDel is slot_tp_finalize: the class's __del__ called, its exception to sys.unraisablehook."] [396 1 "// finalizeGen is _PyGen_Finalize: an async generator with sys's finalizer hook handed to it; a coroutine never"] [397 1 "// started warns; a suspended generator or coroutine closed."] [417 1 "// warnUnawaitedCoroutine is _PyErr_WarnUnawaitedCoroutine: warnings._warn_unawaited_coroutine(coro), or a plain"] [418 1 "// RuntimeWarning when that failed other than by the warning itself."] [423 33 "// get_warnings_attr imports nothing at shutdown (queue 253)"] [450 1 "// finUnraisable is PyErr_FormatUnraisable from a finalizer (the object None)."] [457 1 "// finRound is one round of gc.collect: Go's collection, a wait until Go's finalizer goroutine has run every finalizer"] [458 1 "// it queued (finBarrier), then the drain; the number of dead objects handled."] [467 1 "// finBarrier is the wait after runtime.GC() (queue 316, \"As built: 316\"): until Go's finalizer goroutine has run every"] [468 1 "// finalizer queued so far, or done holds (done nil: never), at most limit. runtime.GC returns with its sweep finished,"] [469 1 "// so every finalizer of its collection is queued by then; runtime/metrics' counts of the finalizers queued and executed"] [470 1 "// (the executed counted once a block of them has run) are equal once all of them ran. A finalizer that does not return"] [471 1 "// (no run counted for 3 ms) ends the wait as the quiet wait it replaces did (218's: 3 ms without a finalizer run)."] [502 1 "// finCollect is gc.collect's finalization: rounds until one handles nothing (at most 8), none when nothing is"] [503 1 "// tracked or queued; then the cycles through finalizers (cyCollect, queue 222) and the rounds again for what their"] [504 1 "// trash held; the number of cyclic trash nodes (CPython's count: acyclic garbage is reference counting's)."] [507 1 "// finCollectAt is finCollect, at the interpreter's end when exit (finExitRounds for the rounds after the cycles)."] [522 1 "// finExitRounds is set by the interpreter's end for the rounds after its cycle collections (exitCollect's second"] [523 1 "// finRounds, and Py_FinalizeEx's finCollect's when gc.callbacks is empty; queue 316): there a round is skipped when no"] [524 1 "// tracked object can be due (finDueLocked). Such a round queues nothing: a dead tracked object without work or weak"] [525 1 "// callbacks only has its record dropped and its plain weak references cleared by its Go finalizer, and the end's next"] [526 1 "// collection does that first, before any Python code of the end runs (it runs in drains, each after a collection) and"] [527 1 "// before its cycle probe (a dead object still under its Go finalizer would hold what it reaches through the probe's"] [528 1 "// collection: so the rounds before a cyCollect keep every round). gc.collect() keeps every round: a program reads"] [529 1 "// its weak references right after it."] [532 1 "// finDueLocked is whether a dead object can be queued at the next collection (finMu held): the queue not empty, or a"] [533 1 "// tracked object with work or weak references with callbacks (exitWorkPending's test, the pending generators left)."] [551 1 "// finRounds is 218's rounds: the dead objects handled."] [554 2 "// the classes' attribute caches out of date are dropped now, not at their next lookup: a stale answer (a method"] [555 2 "// deleted from its class) would keep its value alive"] [579 1 "// finalizeSocket is sock_finalize: an open socket warns ResourceWarning \"unclosed %R\" (its source the socket), then"] [580 1 "// its descriptor is closed."] [597 1 "// resourceWarn is PyErr_ResourceWarning(source, 1, msg): warnings.warn(msg, ResourceWarning, 1, source=source)."] [600 59 "// _warnings' own path at shutdown (queue 253)"] [614 1 "// growStack gives f's value stack room for n more values in a new array, the old one's values cleared: newFrame's one"] [615 1 "// allocation holds the fast locals and the stack's first array together, so the stack's stale values there would keep"] [616 1 "// their objects reachable through the fast locals for the frame's life (queue 218: found by a weak reference that a"] [617 1 "// function's first call did not clear)."] [626 1 "// pendingGens are the coroutines made, and the generators suspended in a try region, since the last flush (under the"] [627 1 "// GIL): one still not finished when the list is flushed (every 256, and in gc.collect) is tracked for its finalization,"] [628 1 "// so the common cases, a coroutine awaited at once and a generator run to its end, pay no Go finalizer (queue 218:"] [629 1 "// measured with bin/pyi aot, a coroutine 0.13 us untracked against 0.6 us tracked at creation; a generator with a"] [630 1 "// try 0.66 us against 1.0-1.2 us tracked at its first suspension)."] [641 1 "// track tracks a generator not finished for its finalization. Its frame's pointer back at it becomes an address: Go"] [642 1 "// never finalizes an object that reaches itself (queue 224: no suspended generator's frame let its generator die, so"] [643 1 "// neither close nor \"never awaited\" ran)."] [653 1 "// The moment at a call's return (queue 297; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 297\"): CPython's reference counting"] [654 1 "// frees a generator a call leaves suspended when the call drops its last reference (next(gen()), any(gen())): its"] [655 1 "// close then (GeneratorExit thrown in, finally blocks and a monitor's events), its frame's locals with it. pyi knows that"] [656 1 "// moment without a collection when the generator's only holder was the value stack: made by the calling frame's"] [657 1 "// previous instruction (stampGen: the frame's address and instruction, and callSeq, every call counting itself, so no"] [658 1 "// call ran between), not handed out since (f_generator marks it exposed), and the last argument of a consumer that"] [659 1 "// keeps no reference to its arguments (Builtin.dropsArg: next, any, all, min, max, sum, sorted). No instruction ran"] [660 1 "// between its making and the consumer's call, so nothing stored it; the consumer kept nothing; its own frame does not"] [661 1 "// hold it (a frame object does not keep its generator alive in CPython either). dropGen closes it at the return. Cost:"] [662 1 "// an increment per call and a flag test per built-in call; a collection only for its frame's locals with a finalizer"] [663 1 "// due (222's moment, as del's)."] [665 1 "// callSeq counts the calls (callStack, AotCallV, AotCallMethodV; queue 297)."] [668 1 "// stampGen stamps o, a generator just made by f's running instruction, with its making."] [675 1 "// freshGen is o when it is a generator not yet run, made by f's previous instruction with no call since (the call at"] [676 1 "// callSeq n0 the next one) and never handed out: held by the value stack alone, and now by the consumer's arguments."] [686 1 "// dropGen is the consumer's return for a fresh generator g: suspended, it dies now (_PyGen_Finalize: close, its error"] [687 1 "// to sys.unraisablehook), and its frame's locals with a finalizer due are checked at once (222's finDeleted)."] [689 62 "// exposed: f_generator handed out while it ran"] [694 20 "// a frame object handed out before the close (the close's own GeneratorExit traceback is dropped)"] [700 13 "// no frame object held elsewhere: its locals cleared, as _PyFrame_ClearExceptCode's"] [707 2 "// their collections held to a tenth of the wall time of their own (genSpent), apart from del's (finSpent)"] [716 1 "// genSpent is dropGen's collections' time (its locals' checks), held as finSpent is, apart from it."] [719 1 "// scrubSlots is n nested calls, each a window of 16 interface slots that goi clears at a call's entry: under stage 0's"] [720 1 "// goi a returned call's slots above the stack's top keep their values (the checkout's goi clears them since c9047d52),"] [721 1 "// here the closed frame's locals; compiled, nanoseconds."] [731 1 "// genLocalsDue are the addresses of the tracked objects with work or weak references due that f's fast locals and"] [732 1 "// cells hold (at most 4), read before f is dropped."] [761 1 "// generator is f's generator (f.f_generator), nil when none, or when it died first."] [788 1 "// Cycles through finalizers (queue 222; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 222\"): Go never frees a cycle that"] [789 1 "// reaches a finalized object from itself, so gc.collect() finds them as CPython's gc_collect_main does, with Go's"] [790 1 "// collector answering what deduce_unreachable's counts answer: which objects are held from outside. The graph's nodes"] [791 1 "// are instances (their dictionary, while not handed out as an object, and __slots__ folded in), lists, tuples and"] [792 1 "// dictionaries; its edges their slots of interface type that hold a node. Every edge between two probed nodes is"] [793 1 "// hidden (the slot set to nil, its target kept by address), each probed node given a probe's Go finalizer, and Go"] [794 1 "// collects with the GIL held: a node whose probe does not run is held from outside, and so is what it reaches."] [797 22 "// gc.DEBUG_SAVEALL"] [798 2 "// gcDebugUncollectable is gc.DEBUG_UNCOLLECTABLE (the shutdown's garbage list printed, queue 253)"] [800 33 "// a larger graph is left alone (Go's collection, 218's moment)"] [804 35 "// a probe's answer is being read (finMu): a probe that runs later only holds"] [805 35 "// the probed nodes whose probe ran (finMu), held until the collection ends"] [806 35 "// those that ran after the answer was read"] [807 35 "// tracemalloc traced once: a list, a dict or a cell may carry its Go finalizer"] [808 35 "// gc.set_debug's flags"] [809 35 "// gc.garbage"] [810 2 "// gcCollecting: a gc.collect() runs (gc.collecting: faulthandler's \"Garbage-collecting\" line, queue 241)"] [814 1 "// cyNode is a node of the graph, never holding its object (its address is hidden from the collector)."] [818 18 "// its record when tracked"] [819 18 "// its slots that hold a node, by address: a slot in the node itself (a FutureIter's) must not hold it"] [820 18 "// in step: the slot is a typed pointer (*Dict, *Cell ...), else an Object"] [821 18 "// the nodes they hold, in step"] [828 1 "// cyLeaves are the objects a collection's graph does not walk (queue 241): the dictionaries of the modules sys.modules"] [829 1 "// holds and the builtins' (held from outside: walking them would walk the whole program), and the frames running on a"] [830 1 "// thread's stack (their slots change under the loop; their Go frames hold them). Set by cyCollect, nil otherwise."] [833 1 "// cySetLeaves computes cyLeaves for this collection."] [877 1 "// cyIsNode is whether o is a node: an object whose references cyTraverse lists (CPython's tp_traverse), not a leaf of"] [878 1 "// this collection (cyLeaves), and able to take a probe's Go finalizer (a list's, a dictionary's or a cell's Go finalizer"] [879 1 "// may be tracemalloc's once it traced: then none of them)."] [892 3 "// a frame a Python object may hold (a traceback's, f_back's, gi_frame's), not running on a thre