o find."] [1263 1 "// cyProbe asks Go's collector which of the nodes in are held from outside the set: the edges between them hidden, a"] [1264 1 "// probe's finalizer on each (a tracked node's own taken off), runtime.GC() with the GIL held, a wait until every"] [1265 1 "// probe ran or Go's finalizers have all run (finBarrier); then the slots put back and the probes taken off. The answer: the nodes"] [1266 1 "// reachable (held from outside, or reached from such a node through the edges)."] [1286 2 "// with its probe set each node outlives its last reference: what an earlier probe held is let go now"] [1374 1 "// cyHideRegistries takes the probed nodes out of the runtime's registries that hold their keys where CPython holds"] [1375 1 "// nothing (queue 241, \"Design: 241\": the weak registries): id()'s identities of untracked objects and the functions'"] [1376 1 "// annotations. The returned function puts back the reachable nodes' entries once the answer is read; the trash's go"] [1377 1 "// (a tracked node's identity into its record), so that Go can free it."] [1411 22 "// the trash's identity in its record, should a finalizer resurrect it"] [1422 1 "// cyDebug (PYI_GC_DEBUG=1): each probe prints to stderr its nodes held from outside that no other probed node holds,"] [1423 1 "// the roots of what it keeps (queue 241: what to look at when a cycle is not found)."] [1458 1 "// cySetFinalizer gives n's object the probe's Go finalizer (a tracked node's own taken off first: Go allows one)."] [1467 1 "// cyRestore gives a surviving tracked node its own Go finalizer again (its record dropped when it needs none)."] [1484 1 "// cyClearWeakRefs clears the weak references to the trash's tracked nodes (handle_weakrefs): their callbacks, in each"] [1485 1 "// list's order, returned to be called once all are cleared (a weak reference is never a node: always \"outside\")."] [1497 24 "// a weak reference in the trash itself: no callback (handle_weakrefs)"] [1509 1 "// cyCollect is gc.collect()'s cycle detection: the trash found, PEP 442's order run over it; the number of trash nodes."] [1526 2 "// the trash in CPython's lists' order (cyOrder, queue 253): the finalizers and callbacks in a fixed order"] [1572 1 "// cySeq is a node's record's order, the untracked last."] [1580 1 "// cyCount is the probed nodes whose probe ran (finMu held)."] [1600 1 "// cyFind is the cyclic trash: from the tracked nodes (or, only given, from those nodes alone: the resurrection's"] [1601 1 "// check), the graph, its relevant part probed; every probed node restored but the trash's (they keep no Go finalizer)."] [1624 1 "// cyOrder is the trash in the order CPython's lists would hold it (queue 253): its collector moves what a container"] [1625 1 "// reaches behind the container, so the trash runs from what nothing else in it holds (the dead module dictionaries"] [1626 1 "// first, in sys.modules' order, then by the records' order) through the references in their slots' order, breadth"] [1627 1 "// first; a cycle nothing outside it holds starts at its oldest record. A wrapper is finalized before what it wraps"] [1628 1 "// (an unclosed text file flushes its buffer before its raw file closes)."] [1693 1 "// cySeedGraph builds the graph and its relevant part in a frame of its own, so no object of the walk stays in a live"] [1694 1 "// variable of the probe's caller."] [1735 3 "// a dead module dictionary and all it reaches are probed (queue 253)"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[95 28] [115 28] [157 16] [157 27] [211 21] [219 27] [263 21] [310 16] [359 29] [379 51] [391 42] [403 55] [412 24] [422 25] [433 64] [444 92] [452 25] [476 15] [476 17] [486 28] [563 16] [563 27] [586 51] [591 16] [599 25] [670 28] [735 12] [735 42] [739 40] [742 24] [769 21] [854 33] [867 19] [867 29] [934 13] [944 13] [949 13] [954 13] [959 13] [964 13] [969 13] [974 13] [979 13] [1006 17] [1031 26] [1104 18] [1130 21] [1134 23] [1147 12] [1147 28] [1153 18] [1182 22] [11